  "instance_name": "religious_penitence_stereotype",
  "label": "Stereotype of religious penitence",
  "description": "The image of children carrying crosses evokes the stereotype of religious penitence, particularly associated with Catholic traditions like the Way of the Cross or Holy Week processions. This stereotype is often used to depict religious practice as extreme, self-flagellating, or overly rigid. The meme uses this stereotype to imply that religious upbringing is similarly extreme or harmful, even though the image may not depict actual religious rituals.",
